{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/kind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"kind","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV4kindAA23MXLStartStopDiscontinueOvp"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/kind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this ending starts, stops, or discontinues, determining which barline it is associated with and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether a downward jog is drawn."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/kind":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/kind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this ending starts, stops, or discontinues, determining which barline it is associated with and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether a downward jog is drawn."}],"title":"kind","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopDiscontinue":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue","abstract":[{"text":"The start-stop-discontinue type is used to specify ending types. Typically, the start type is associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a downward","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is typical for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"second endings that do not conclude a piece.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","abstract":[{"text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLEnding","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","kind":"symbol"}}}